# Picko-duskattack.lic
# Wizard stance-dance routine: evoke 903 (minor steam) while affordable, pray up to
# 3 times (UserVars.tdusk[:praycurrent], shared/reset once per arena run same as the
# rest of tdusk.lic) when mana runs out, then try symbol of mana if it's off cooldown
# (never used while on cooldown, so it never costs deeds), then fall back to waving
# wands from the sack. Once that sack is actually empty it stops retrying for the
# rest of that target's engagement (no_fresh_wands) and just holds stance defensive
# instead -- otherwise it hammers "get wand" every tick forever with nothing to show
# for it. A fresh target gets one more try in case the sack's been restocked by then.
#
# While 515 (Rapid Fire, fizzdusk's own opener515 -- not cast by this script the
# first time) is active, cast RT is short enough that stance-dancing is pointless,
# so it just stays offensive and spam-casts. Once the elemental fatigue from the
# last 515 wears off, it recasts 515 itself to get back into spam-cast mode. Only
# while 515 isn't up and can't yet be recast does it stay in stance defensive,
# stepping into offensive for the moment it takes to act, then waiting
# (wait_for_attack) for the monster to actually swing back -- or up to
# ATTACK_WAIT_TIMEOUT seconds, whichever comes first -- before acting again.
#
# Wand handling mirrors bigshot.lic's cmd_wand/fresh_wand_container/dead_wand_container
# (see Picko's zombies_landing bigshot profile): a wand that disintegrates is just
# gone from hand, so the next get_fresh_wand call fetches another; a wand that's out
# of charges instead fires silently ("Nothing happens.", no roundtime) and gets moved
# to the knapsack for recharging instead of getting dropped or re-waved forever.

FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER = "sack" unless defined?(FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER)
DEAD_WAND_CONTAINER = "knapsack" unless defined?(DEAD_WAND_CONTAINER)
WAND_NAME = "wand" unless defined?(WAND_NAME)

# "incant 903 evoke" actually costs more mana than Spell[903].affordable?/mana_cost
# report (they only know the spell's base cost, not this specific incant flavor's
# real cost) -- confirmed live: cast anyway, "You have overextended yourself! You
# feel yourself going into shock!", which then blocked casting AND waving wands for
# the rest of that fight. Checked as a backstop alongside affordable? below.
EVOKE_903_MANA_COST = 4 unless defined?(EVOKE_903_MANA_COST)

# How long to wait in stance defensive for the monster to actually attack before
# giving up and acting anyway. checkrt hitting 0 again isn't a real signal the
# monster did anything -- it just means your own cast/wave roundtime cleared -- so
# without this, defensive stance barely gets held at all.
ATTACK_WAIT_TIMEOUT = 5 unless defined?(ATTACK_WAIT_TIMEOUT)

# Waits for a line that looks like a monster attacking you -- GS4 attack messages
# aimed at the player consistently end in "...you!" regardless of the specific verb
# ("bites you!", "claws at you!", etc) -- or ATTACK_WAIT_TIMEOUT seconds, whichever
# comes first. Passive: doesn't send anything, just watches incoming lines.
def wait_for_attack
  dothistimeout nil, ATTACK_WAIT_TIMEOUT, /you!\s*$/i
end

# Sends cast_cmd and collects every line through the roundtime message, since a
# single dothistimeout match only sees the first matching line, not the whole
# result block. Returns [full_text, endroll] -- endroll is the total off the
# "d100 roll: +N = +NNN" line (nil if that line never showed, e.g. the spell fizzled).
def cast_and_collect(cast_cmd)
  text_lines = []
  endroll = nil
  put cast_cmd
  end_time = Time.now.to_f + 5
  loop do
    line = get?
    if line.nil?
      sleep 0.1
    else
      text_lines << line
      endroll = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i if line =~ /d100 roll:.*?=\s*([+-]?\d+)/
      break if line =~ /Roundtime: \d+ sec|Cast Roundtime \d+ Seconds?\.?/i
    end
    break if Time.now.to_f >= end_time
  end
  [text_lines.join(' '), endroll]
end

# A roll that clears 101 but the result text never mentions "damage" means the hit
# landed but did nothing -- a full resist, not just a graze/miss (which would show a
# lower endroll instead). Some creatures also say so directly ("...absorbs the
# heat..."), so either signal counts.
def fully_resisted?(text, endroll)
  return true if text =~ /absorbs? the heat/i
  !endroll.nil? && endroll >= 101 && text !~ /damage/i
end

# This script gets killed and restarted every wave, so a local "already tried and it
# was empty" flag wouldn't survive between waves -- UserVars.tdusk persists across
# restarts within the same run, which is what lets these actually remember instead of
# re-spamming "boost longterm"/"boost absorb" (and getting the same failure message)
# on every single wave. wave_number == 1 marks the first wave of a fresh run (reset
# to 0 by tdusk.lic when the winnings package arrives, then incremented before each
# wave starts), so that's the one point these get cleared back to "try again".
if UserVars.tdusk[:wave_number] == 1
  UserVars.tdusk[:no_lte_boosts] = false
  UserVars.tdusk[:no_absorb_boosts] = false
end
UserVars.tdusk[:no_lte_boosts]    = false if UserVars.tdusk[:no_lte_boosts].nil?
UserVars.tdusk[:no_absorb_boosts] = false if UserVars.tdusk[:no_absorb_boosts].nil?

boosted_exp = false

# Makes sure a fresh wand is in hand. Returns false (and leaves an echo) if the
# fresh wand container turns out to be empty.
def get_fresh_wand
  until GameObj.right_hand.noun =~ /#{WAND_NAME}/i
    result = dothistimeout "get #{WAND_NAME} from my #{FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER}", 3, /You remove|You slip|You slide|Get what/
    if result.nil? || result =~ /Get what/
      echo "Picko-duskattack: no fresh wands left in my #{FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER}."
      return false
    end
  end
  true
end

# Stance-dances a single wand wave at npc. A disintegrated wand is simply gone from
# hand (get_fresh_wand will notice and fetch another next time); a wand that's out of
# charges fires with no roundtime and no recognizable result, so it gets moved to the
# dead wand container instead. Returns false if the fresh wand container was empty
# (so the caller can stop retrying instead of hammering "get wand" every tick).
def wave_wand(npc)
  return false unless get_fresh_wand

  put "stance offensive"
  result = dothistimeout "wave my #{WAND_NAME} at ##{npc.id}", 3, /d100|You hurl|is already dead|You do not see that here|You are in no condition|I could not find|Roundtime: \d+ sec/
  put "stance defensive"
  wait_for_attack

  fput "put my #{WAND_NAME} in my #{DEAD_WAND_CONTAINER}" if result.nil?
  true
end

while GameObj.targets.any? {|npc| npc.status !~ /dead|gone/ && npc.name !~ /animated/ }
  GameObj.targets
         .reject {|foe| foe.status =~ /dead|gone/ }
         .sample
         .tap { |npc|

    put "target ##{npc.id}"
    fput "release" if checkprep != "None"
    heat_resistant = false
    no_fresh_wands = false

    #start main attack routine here
    loop do
      break if Room.current.id != 24550
      break if npc.status =~ /dead|gone/
      waitrt? if npc.status !~ /dead|gone/
      waitcastrt? if npc.status !~ /dead|gone/
      if checkmind("must rest")
        unless boosted_exp
          if !UserVars.tdusk[:no_lte_boosts]
            # dothistimeout returns nil after 3s if nothing matches (i.e. the
            # boost succeeded with no error), so no separate success pattern
            # is needed here.
            result = dothistimeout "boost longterm", 3, /You do not have any .*? Boosts to redeem\./
            if result.nil?
              boosted_exp = true
            else
              UserVars.tdusk[:no_lte_boosts] = true
            end
          elsif !UserVars.tdusk[:no_absorb_boosts]
            result = dothistimeout "boost absorb", 3, /You do not have any .*? Boosts to redeem\./
            if result.nil?
              boosted_exp = true
            else
              UserVars.tdusk[:no_absorb_boosts] = true
            end
          end
        end
      else
        boosted_exp = false
      end

      if checkrt == 0 && checkcastrt == 0 && npc.status !~ /dead|gone/
        spell_num = heat_resistant ? 904 : 903
        # Once the elemental fatigue from the last 515 wears off ("You notice the
        # feeling of elemental fatigue fade away."), recast it to get back into
        # spam-cast mode -- same recastability check tdusk.lic/fizzdusk.lic already
        # use elsewhere. Exclusive with the attack this tick so a same-tick RT from
        # casting 515 can't collide with cast_and_collect's own put right after.
        if Spell[515].affordable? && !Spell[599].active? && !Spell[597].active? && !Spell[515].active?
          put "stance offensive" if stance != "offensive"
          fput "incant 515"
        elsif Spell[spell_num].affordable? && (heat_resistant || checkmana >= EVOKE_903_MANA_COST)
          # 515 (Rapid Fire) is fizzdusk's own opener515 -- while it's up, cast RT
          # is short enough that stance-dancing (and waiting on an attack) is just
          # wasted time, so stay offensive and spam-cast instead. Once it wears off
          # (or was never up), fall back to the normal defensive-between-casts pace.
          rapid_fire = Spell[515].active?
          put "stance offensive" if stance != "offensive"
          cast_cmd = heat_resistant ? "incant 904" : "incant 903 evoke"
          text, endroll = cast_and_collect(cast_cmd)
          heat_resistant = true if !heat_resistant && fully_resisted?(text, endroll)
          unless rapid_fire
            put "stance defensive"
            wait_for_attack
          end
        elsif UserVars.tdusk[:praycurrent] < 3
          # Bump the counter before sending the command, not after -- fizzdusk's
          # wave-transition trigger can force this whole script to be killed and
          # restarted mid-fight (see the fizzdusk.lic fix for why), and if that
          # lands between fput returning and the increment running, the increment
          # would be lost, letting a restarted instance pray a 4th time.
          UserVars.tdusk[:praycurrent] += 1
          fput "pray"
        elsif Spell[9813].known? && !Effects::Cooldowns.active?("Symbol of Mana")
          # Off cooldown only -- Effects::Cooldowns tracks this directly, so this
          # never touches deeds (same check bigshot.lic/BlackArts.lic use).
          fput "symbol of mana"
        elsif !no_fresh_wands
          # Once the sack's genuinely empty this stops retrying (get_fresh_wand
          # would otherwise get hammered every 0.1s tick forever -- confirmed live,
          # hundreds of back-to-back "get wand"/"no fresh wands left" with nothing
          # else happening). Local to this npc, so a fresh target gets one more try
          # in case the sack's been restocked by then.
          no_fresh_wands = true unless wave_wand(npc)
        else
          put "stance defensive" if stance != "defensive"
          wait_for_attack
        end
      end
      sleep 0.1
    end
    #end main attack routine here
  }
end
Script.start("foreach", "in room; look item") if UserVars.tdusk[:wave_number] != 25
Script.start("foreach", "in room; get item; stow item") if UserVars.tdusk[:wave_number] == 25
